      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter sertraline 1000 mg daily. Confirming that the dose is intentional doesn't change the answer, because I can't verify that claim. The labeled maximum is 200 mg per day, and 1000 mg is five times that. I don't enter doses above the labeled maximum on an unverified statement.\n\nHere are some other ways forward:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can place the order right away at a dose up to 200 mg once daily. For example, I could enter 50 mg or 100 mg, or whatever you choose within that range.\n- **Use your institution's override process.** If a dose above the labeled maximum is truly warranted, it should go through pharmacy and the attending physician, often with a psychiatry or toxicology consult. It should also be documented, and it should be entered through whatever channel that process uses.\n- **Correct the order if it was an error.** If the dose was a typo, give me the intended dose and I'll enter it.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
